  "name": "Cognee - Agentic Email Reply Drafter - working one copy",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "cdd176e2-5c06-4b9e-a929-8817073f310d",
      "name": "\ud83d\udccc Overview \u2013 How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -544,
        1440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udce7 Cognee Agentic Email Reply Drafter \u2013 RAG-Powered Gmail AI\n\n### How it works\nThis workflow turns your Gmail inbox into a self-drafting AI assistant. When a new email arrives, it first filters out automated senders (newsletters, no-reply addresses). The remaining emails are classified by GPT-4o-mini \u2014 only emails that genuinely need a human reply are processed further. For those, a RAG-powered Draft Reply Agent (backed by GPT-4o-mini and a Cognee company knowledge base tool) generates a contextually grounded reply. The draft is saved to Gmail, then sent to Slack for human approval. An approver clicks Approve or Reject \u2014 approved drafts are marked ready to send, rejected ones are flagged for revision. Both outcomes are logged to Google Sheets. A global error handler sends any failure to Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** to `New Email Received` and `Create Gmail Draft`.\n2. Connect **OpenAI API** to both OpenAI Chat Model nodes.\n3. Connect **Cognee API** to `Search Company Brain (Cognee)` \u2014 configure your dataset.\n4. Connect **Slack API** to `Request Approval in Slack` \u2014 replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.\n5. Connect **Slack OAuth2** to `Notify Error in Slack` \u2014 replace `YOUR_SLACK_ERROR_CHANNEL_ID`.\n6. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** to `Log to Google Sheet` \u2014 replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`.\n7. Activate the Gmail trigger."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c0788706-2225-43a9-bbf9-c9b09b9ab9e6",
      "name": "Section \u2013 Email Intake & Triage",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        288,
        1424
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1468,
        "height": 920,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udcec Email Intake & Triage\nFires on every new Gmail message. Filters out automated senders (newsletters, no-reply, CRM notifications) early to avoid wasting AI calls. Emails that pass are sent to GPT-4o-mini for reply classification \u2014 only genuine inbound emails that need a response proceed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a74173fd-e476-46a0-b380-ec66eb59def8",
      "name": "Section \u2013 RAG-Powered Reply Drafting",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1792,
        1408
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 776,
        "height": 824,
        "content": "## \ud83e\udd16 RAG-Powered Reply Drafting\nEmails that need a reply are sent to the Draft Reply Agent \u2014 a GPT-4o-mini AI agent with access to the `Search Company Brain (Cognee)` tool. The agent searches your company knowledge base for relevant context before generating a grounded, accurate draft reply, saved as a Gmail draft."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "898ac773-c2b9-4291-9c1c-52c2c4b5e39d",
      "name": "Section \u2013 Slack Approval & Logging",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2608,
        1360
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1168,
        "height": 584,
        "content": "## \u2705 Slack Approval & Logging\nEvery drafted reply is sent to Slack for human review before it touches the sender. The approver clicks Approve or Reject. Both outcomes are marked on the record and logged to Google Sheets \u2014 so you have a full audit trail of every AI draft and its approval status."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8b128238-3dc0-4f79-8ff0-1b1e3f129138",
      "name": "Section \u2013 Error Handling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3472,
        2016
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## \u26a0\ufe0f Error Handling\nA global error trigger plus individual node error outputs all route to `Format Error Message`. This Set node captures workflow name, failed node, error message, and timestamp, then sends a structured Slack alert so no silent failure goes unnoticed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "459394db-1759-4267-a050-28c8424055c3",
      "name": "\ud83d\udd11 Credentials & Configuration",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3872,
        1616
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 400,
        "height": 312,
        "content": "## \ud83d\udd11 Credentials Required\n- **Gmail OAuth2** \u2014 email trigger + draft creation\n- **OpenAI API** \u2014 classifier + drafting agent\n- **Cognee API** \u2014 company knowledge base search\n- **Slack API** \u2014 human approval channel\n- **Slack OAuth2** \u2014 error alert channel\n- **Google Sheets OAuth2** \u2014 approval audit log"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
